{"name":"Allegro","hex":"#b28959","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"allegro","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A tempo mark directing that a passage is to be played in a quick, lively tempo, faster than allegretto but slower than presto.","An expressive mark indicating that a passage is to be played in a lively or happy manner, not necessarily quickly."]},{"part":"Adverb","definitions":["played in a quick, lively tempo"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/allegro"}],"entries":[{"title":"Tempo","blocks":[{"text":"In musical terminology, tempo, measured in beats per minute, is the speed or pace of a given composition, and is often also an indication of the composition's character or atmosphere. In classical music, tempo is typically indicated with an instruction at the start of a piece and, if a specific metrical pace is desired, is usually measured in beats per minute. In modern classical compositions, a \"metronome mark\" in beats per minute, indicating only measured speed and not any form of expression, may supplement or replace the normal tempo marking, while in modern genres like electronic dance music, tempo will typically simply be stated in bpm."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/85/Tempo_plots.svg/330px-Tempo_plots.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tempo","wikidata":"Q189214"},{"title":"Glossary of ballet","blocks":[{"text":"Because ballet became formalized in France, a significant part of ballet terminology is in the French language."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Glossary_of_ballet","wikidata":"Q805240"},{"title":"Allegro (website)","blocks":[{"text":"Allegro is a Polish online marketplace and e-commerce platform headquartered in Poznań. It is the largest e-commerce platform in Poland and operates marketplaces in Poland, the Czech Republic, Slovakia and Hungary. The platform is operated by Allegro sp. z o.o., while its parent company, Allegro.eu S.A., is incorporated in Luxembourg and listed on the Warsaw Stock Exchange."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8b/2015_Woodstock_052_allegro_-_diabelski_m%C5%82yn.jpg/330px-2015_Woodstock_052_allegro_-_diabelski_m%C5%82yn.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Allegro_(website)","wikidata":"Q58014"},{"title":"Allegro (software library)","blocks":[{"text":"Allegro is a software library for video game development. The functionality of the library includes support for basic 2D graphics, image manipulation, text output, audio output, MIDI music, input and timers, as well as additional routines for fixed-point and floating-point matrix arithmetic, Unicode strings, file system access, file manipulation, data files, and 3D graphics. The library is written in the C programming language and designed to be used with C, C++, or Objective-C, with bindings available for Python, Lua, Scheme, D, Go, and other languages. Allegro comes with extensive documentation and many examples."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/a/a8/Allegro-logo.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Allegro_(software_library)","wikidata":"Q1503415"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/29/Electronic-metronome%28scale%29.jpg/500px-Electronic-metronome%28scale%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/29/Electronic-metronome%28scale%29.jpg/500px-Electronic-metronome%28scale%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Wittner electronic metronome","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AElectronic-metronome(scale).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/comm